$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Fluoro-N-(2-hydroxyphenyl)-benzamide (5b)
(500 mg, 2.16 mmol) was dissolved in DMF (10 mL), and one equivalent of
freshly powdered NaOH was added. The resulting mixture was heated at
reflux for 5 h After cooling to room temperature, the mixture was diluted
with water (100 mL), and the precipitated product was filtered over a
glass filter and washed with 5% NaOH and then water to remove the
unreacted starting material. The solid residue was dried overnight under
vacuum and was used in the next step without further purification. Yield
320 mg (70%). 7-Chloro-4-fluoro-dibenzo[b,f][1,4]oxazepin-11(10H )-one
(6m) Synthesized from 6m by the general method described for 6b. Yield
3.84 g (81%). Mp 285-293°C; 1H NMR (DMSO-d6) δ (ppm) 10.78 (bs, 1H), 7.60
(m, 2H), 7.37 (m, 3H), 7.21 (d, J=8.6 Hz, 1H).
