$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4p, 4m, and 4o. A 5.80 g (0.021 mol) sample of 3p, 3.0 g
(0.021 mol) of 4-nitrofluorobenzene, 15 g (0.1 mol) of CsF, and 60 mL of
DMF were heated together at 100 °C for 24 h. After cooling to room
temperature, the mixture was poured into 1 L of cold, dilute hydrochloric
acid. The product was collected by filtration, washed with dilute
hydrochloric acid, and dried in a vacuum. After recrystallization from
aqueous acetic acid, 4pwas obtained. Yield 6.8 g, 81%. Mp: 218-220 °C. 1H
NMR (DMSO-d6, ppm): δ 8.276-8.246 (m, 2H), 8.108-8.078 (d, 1H),
7.639-7.581 (m, 3H), 7.261-7.230 (m, 2H), 7.145-7.087 (m, 3H). IR (KBr):
3370, 1713, 1689, 1597, 1578, 1508, 1500, 1489, 1418, 1342, 1290, 1257,
