$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
nitrophenoxybenzenes Phenol (1 molar eq.), 1-fluoro-4-nitrobenzene (2
molar eq.), and Na2CO3 (2 molar eq.), were suspended in DMF (3.5 mL) and
heated. The reaction was followed by TLC, hexane : diethyl ether (9:1),
and after completion (approximately 3-6 h), the desired product was
extracted with dichloromethane (3×50 mL). The crude product was purified
by flash chromatography, hexane : diethyl ether (100:1).
1-Nitro-4-(3-(trifluoromethoxy)phenoxy)benzene, 7c Yellow oil; 81%. 1H
NMR (CD3OD, 400.13 MHz) δ 7.09-7.22 (5H, m, Ar-H); 7.56 (1H, m, Ar-H);
8.28 (2H, d, J = 9.2 Hz, Ar-H).
