$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 4-fluorobenzaldehyde (2.92 g, 23.6 mmol, 1.00 equiv.)
and 4-bromo-2-chlorophenol (5.13 g, 24.7 mmol, 1.05 equiv.) in DMSO (100
mL) under N2 was added KF on Al2O3 (4.79 g, 33.0 mmol, 1.40 equiv.) and
18-crown-6 (620 mg, 2.36 mmol, 0.100 equiv.) at room temperature. The
reaction mixture was heated at 110 °C for 40 h. The reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature and diluted with water (200 mL) and ethyl
acetate (100 mL). The phases were separated, and the aqueous layer was
extracted with ethyl acetate (100 mL × 2). The combined organic phases
were washed with brine (100 mL), dried over sodium sulfate, filtered, and
concentrated in vacuo to afford a brown oil. The crude product was
purified by silica gel column chromatography (ethyl acetate/hexanes =
1/24). The title compound as a yellow oil (5.93 g, 81%). The title
compound, contaminated with ~5% of an unidentified species that could not
be separated from S11, was used directly in the next step. 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.91 (s, 1H), 7.84 (d, J = 9 Hz, 2H), 7.63 (d, J = 2 Hz,
1H), 7.42 (dd, J = 9, 2 Hz, 1H), 6.97-7.02 (m, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 190.7, 162.0, 150.0, 133.8, 132.2, 131.9, 131.7, 128.3, 124.0,
118.5, 117.0 ppm. IR: 3086, 2826, 2736, 1734, 1695, 1600, 1585, 1575,
1501, 1467, 1373, 1256, 1235, 1209, 1080, 1058, 826, 732, 696, 636, 616
cm-1. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd. for C13H9BrClO2 [M+H+]: 310.9469; found
310.9474.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Virtually Instantaneous, Room-Temperature [11C]-Cyanation Using Biaryl
Phosphine Pd(0) Complexes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
