$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3,5-Dibromo-2-(2,4-dibromophenoxy)-benzaldehyde (21):
3,5-Dibromosalicylaldehyde (0.704 g, 2.5 mmol) and sodium hydroxide
(0.120 g, 3.0 mmol) were dissolved in 1,4-dioxane (15 mL) and water (15
mL). 11 (1.90 g, 3.0 mmol) was added and then the reaction mixture was
heated to 8°C. After stirring for 90 minutes, the solution was cooled to
room temperature and diluted with water (30 mL) and methylene chloride
(30 mL). The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted
with methylene chloride (50 mL, 3x). The organic fractions were combined,
washed with aqueous sodium hydroxide (1.0 M, 50 mL, 2x) and water (50 mL,
2x), and then dried over Na2SO4. The solvents were removed in vacuo.
Flash column chromatography (3:2 hexanes:CH2Cl2). The desired product
(1.03 g, 80%) as a white powder. 1H NMR (500 NMR, CDCl3) δ = 10.06 (s,
1H, CHO), 8.06 (s, 2H, 4-H, 6-H), 7.82 (d, J = 2.5, 1H, 3’-H), 7.29 (dd,
J = 2.5,9.0, 1H, 5’-H), 6.29 (d, J = 9.0, 1H, 6’-H) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Photochemical Formation of Halogenated Dioxins from Hydroxylated
Polybrominated Diphenyl Ethers (OH-PBDEs) and Chlorinated Derivatives
(OH-PBCDEs)
