$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 8-Chloro-10H-dibenzo[b,1][1,4]oxazepin-11-one: Cs2CO3 (7.43 g, 23 mmol)
was added to a solution of 4-chloro-1-fluoro-2-nitrobenzene (2.00 g, 11
mmol) and methyl salicylate (2.92 ml, 23 mmol) in DMF (25 ml) and the
resulting mixture was stirred for 2 hours at 60 °C. The reaction mixture
was cooled to room temperature and diluted with DCM (60 ml). The organic
phase was washed with water and then dried (Na2SO4). Filtration, removal
of the solvent at reduced pressure gave 2.80 g (80%) of the crude
product, which was sufficiently pure to be used in the next step without
further purification.
