$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of Diaryl
Ethers: An oven-dried test tube, which was equipped with a magnetic stir
bar and fitted with a teflon screw-cap, was charged with L8 (1.5-7.5 mol
%), [(cinnamyl)PdCl]2 (0.5-2.5 mol %), K3PO4 (318 mg, 1.5 mmol), aryl
halide (1.0 mmol) and phenol (1.5 mmol). The vessel was evacuated and
backfilled with argon (this process was repeated a total of three times)
after which toluene and DME were added via syringe (the amount of solvent
is specific to each substrate). The solution was stirred at the specified
temperature for 16 h after which it was cooled to rt and diluted with
ethyl acetate, washed with water, filtered through a pad of silica gel
(eluted with diethyl ether), and concentrated under reduced pressure. The
crude material was purified by flash chromatography via the Biotage SP4.
1-isopropyl-2-(4-methoxyphenoxy)benzene (15).14,15 Following the General
Procedure, a mixture of 4-bromo-anisole (125 μL, 1.0 mmol),
2-isopropylphneol (190 μL, 1.5 mmol), L8 (1.5 mol %), [(C6H9)PdCl]2 (0.5
mol %), K3PO4 (318 mg), toluene (0.6 mL) and DME (0.3 mL) was stirred at
80 °C for 24 h. The crude product was purified via the Biotage SP4
(silica-packed 25 g snap column; 0-5% EtOAc/hexanes) to provide the title
compound as a colorless oil (190 mg, 78%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
7.33 (dd, J = 7.3, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 7.15 - 7.03 (m, 2H), 6.96 - 6.84 (m, 4H),
6.80 (dd, J = 7.7, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 3.79 (s, 3H), 3.44 - 3.32 (m, 1H), 1.27
(d, J = 6.9 Hz, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 155.5, 155.1, 151.6,
139.5, 127.0, 126.9, 123.5, 119.6, 118.4, 114.9, 55.8, 27.3, 23.1 ppm. IR
(neat, cm-1): 3032, 2962, 2869, 2834, 2363, 2340, 2037, 1868, 1734, 1717,
1684, 1652, 1581, 1558, 1505, 1449, 1383, 1362, 1345, 1295, 1227, 1180,
1101, 1084, 1037, 1007, 939 cm-1. Anal. Calcd. for C16H18O2: C, 79.31; H,
7.49. Found: C, 79.49; H, 7.60.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A New Biarylphosphine Ligand for the Pd-Catalyzed Synthesis of Diaryl
Ethers under Mild Conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Salvi, Luca; Davis, Nicole R.; Ali, Siraj Z.; Buchwald, Stephen L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(1), 170-173

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME178 STEP1
