$DATUM 123-91-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Experimental Procedure. An oven-dried
resealable Schlenk tube was fitted with a rubber septum and was cooled to
room temperature under N2 purge. The septum was removed, and the tube was
charged with CuI (10 mol%), 10- 50 mg Raney Ni-Al alloy, K2CO3 (2.0
mmol), aryl halides (1.0mmol), and phenols (1.2-1.4 mmol). The tube was
capped with the septum and purged with N2, and then dioxane(2ml) was
added through the septum. The reaction mixture was stirred at 110 °C for
12-24 h (reaction times were not optimized). The reaction mixture was
allowed to cool to room temperature and then diluted with ether and
poured into a separating funnel. The mixture was washed with 1 M NaOH and
brine, and then the organic fraction was dried over anhydrous magnesium
sulfate, filtered, and concentrated. The crude material was purified by
flash chromatography on silical gel. Entry 4, yield 80%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Raney nickel used, DMF or NMP alternately used as solvents, Cs2CO3
alternately used as reagent, CuCl or CuBr alternately used as cocatalyst,
larger amts. of alloy gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly efficient C-O cross-coupling reactions with inactivated halides by
ligandless, heterogeneous raney Ni-Al alloy/copper(I) salts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Xu, Li-Wen; Xia, Chun-Gu; Li, Jing-Wei; Hu, Xiao-Xue
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2003), (13), 2071-2073

