$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bis(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)ether 7a: In a sealed tube, a suspension of
4-iodoveratrole (263 mg, 1.0 mmol), 3,4-dimethoxyphenol (231 mg, 1.5
mmol), Cs2CO3 (650 mg, 2 mmol), CuI (19 mg, 0.1 mmol), N,Ndimethylglycine
hydrochloride (42 mg, 0.3 mmol) in dioxane (2 ml) was stirred at 110 °C
for 20 h under argon atmosphere. Subsequently, aqueous ammonium chloride
(saturated, 30 ml) was added and the mixture was extracted with
dichloromethane (3x50 ml). The solution was dried with magnesium sulfate
and the solvents were evaporated. The crude product was purified by flash
column chromatography (eluent: dichloromethane) to yield compound 7a.
Colorless crystalline solid, yield 233 mg, 80%. mp = 93.7 °C. 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.79 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 6.62 (d, J = 2.7 Hz, 2H), 6.49
(dd, J = 8.7, 2.7 Hz, 2H), 3.86 (s, 6H), 3.82 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 151.74, 149.95, 145.09, 111.81, 109.55, 103.61, 56.42, 56.05.
HRMS (ESI+) m/z calcd for C16H18O5Na [M+Na]+ 313.1052, found 313.1059.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Versatile Oxidative Approach to Carbazoles and Related Compounds Using
MoCl5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Trosien, Simon; Boettger, Philipp; Waldvogel, Siegfried R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(2), 402-405

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME204 STEP1
$RXN



