$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Tricyclic Derivatives 9, 10 (GP
5). 8-Methoxy-2-nitro-10H-dibenzo[b,f][1,4]oxazepin-11-one (9) Amide 7
(2.52 g, 7.81 mmol) was suspended in H2O (65 mL) and an aq. 2 M NaOH
solution (5 mL) was added. The mixture was refluxed for 8 h and then left
to stand at r. t. overnight. The reaction mixture was then poured into
H2O (200 mL), the solid filtered off and the oxazepinone derivative 9
(1.72 g, 80%) was obtained as a brown solid. HPLC: (A) 3.8 min, 98%
purity. 8-Methoxy-2-nitro-10H-dibenzo[b,f][1,4]oxazepin-11-one (9), yield
(1.72 g, 80%) 1H NMR (200 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ (ppm) 10.78 (br s, 1H),
8.51-8.40 (m, 2H), 7.57 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 7.31 (d, J = 9.4 Hz, 1H),
6.75-6.69 (m, 2H), 3.71 (s, 3H). MS (ESI), m/z: 287.1 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
