$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the linear trimer: To a
solution of 1,5-difluoro-2,4-dinitrobenzene (1.68gr, 8.24 mmol) and
resorcinol derivative (2.75 mmol) in acetone (25 ml) was added K2CO3
(1.51gr, 11.0 mmol). The solution was stirred at r.t. for 6 hrs, then
potassium carbonate was filtered out. After most of the solvent was
removed under reduced pressure, the residue was dissolved in CHCl3, and
then washed with saturated solution of NH4Cl, dried over MgSO4, filtered,
and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography
(hexane:EA 7:3). The product as pale yellow solid in 70-80% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM glovebox used
