$DATUM 4-[4-(4-amino-3-methylphenoxy)benzenesulfonyl]-4’-[4-(3-aminophenoxy)benzenesulfonyl]biphenyl
(15). A mixture of 4-amino-m-cresol (0.15 g, 1.2 mmol),
4-(4-chlorobenzenesulfonyl)-4’-[4’’-(3-aminophenoxy)benzenesulfonyl]biphenyl
(0.68 g, 1.2 mmol), potassium carbonate (0.17 g, 1.2 mmol), S6DMAc (10
mL) and toluene (20 mL) was heated to reflux under nitrogen, with
Dean-Stark distillation of water. After 3 h the toluene was distilled off
and the temperature was raised to 160 °C. After a further 4 h, the
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, poured into water (100
mL), filtered. After washing with water and then methanol, the solid was
dried at 100 °C for 2 h and purified by chromatography (dichloromethane
to 1% methanol in dichloromethane) to give a white solid. Yield: 0.63 g,
80%
4-[4-(4-amino-3-methylphenoxy)benzenesulfonyl]-4’-[4-(3-aminophenoxy)benzenesulfonyl]biphenyl
(15), Yield 80% m.p. 255°C ; 1H NMR (CDCl3/hexafluoropropan-2-ol 6:1 v/v,
250 MHz) δ 7.95 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 4H), 7.85 (d, J = 8.8Hz, 2H), 7.83 (d, J
= 8.8Hz, 2H), 7.71 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 4H), 7.28 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.07
(d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.02 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 6.96 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H),
6.89 (t, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H), 6.83 (dd, J = 8.4 and 2.6 Hz, 1H), 6.72 (dd, J
= 8.1 and 2.1 Hz, 1H), 6.67 (dd, J = 8.1 and 2.1 Hz, 1H), 6.54 (t, J =
2.1 Hz, 1H), 2.44(s, 3H), 2.23 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (DMSO-d6, 62.5 MHz) δ
163.8, 162.3, 155.7, 151.2, 144.8, 144.1, 143.4, 143.3, 142.0, 141.8,
134.3, 133.5, 130.8, 130.5, 130.4, 129.0, 128.2, 128.1, 123.2, 122.6,
119.2, 118.1, 116.9, 115.1, 111.1, 107.2, 105.3, 17.8; IR (Nujol): 3473,
3375 (νN-H), 1316., 1249 (νC-O-C), 875, 835, 823; MS (CI): ): m/z = 662
[M]+; Anal. calcd. for C37H30N2O6S2: C 67.05, H 4.56, N 4.23%; found : C
66.83, H 4.57, N 4.02%
