$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Coupling Reaction of Diphenyl Ether (under Microwave Irradiation)
for 10a, 10c, 11c, and 11d. A mixture of 4-substituted
N1-(4-cyanophenyl)-5-chloro-2-nitroaniline (1 equiv, 7 or 9) and
para-substituted 2,6-dimethylphenol (1.2 equiv) in DMF (3 mL) in the
presence of anhydrous potassium carbonate (2 equiv) was irradiated under
microwave conditions with stirring at 190 °C for 15 min. The mixture was
poured into ice-water, adjusted to neutral pH with aqueous HCl (5%), and
extracted with EtOAc three times. After removal of organic solvent under
reduced pressure, crude product was purified by PTLC or flash column
chromatography (gradual eluant, petroleum ether/CH2Cl2).
N1-(4'-Cyanophenyl)-5-(2",6"-dimethyl-4"-formylphenoxy)-4-trifluoromethyl-2-nitroaniline
(10a). Starting with 171 mg (0.5 mmol) of 7 and 90 mg (0.6 mmol) of
2,6-dimethyl-p-formylphenol to afford 182 mg of 10a, yield 80%, yellow
solid. mp 192-194 °C; 1H NMR δ ppm 2.21 (6H, s, 2 × CH3), 6.24 (1H, s,
ArH-6), 7.08 (2H, d, J= 8.4 Hz, ArH-2',6'), 7.51 (2H, d, J= 8.4 Hz,
ArH-3',5'), 7.67 (2H, s, ArH-3",5"), 8.68 (1H, s, ArH-3), 9.92 (1H, s,
NH), 9.97 (1H, s, CHO); MS m/z (%) 456.4 (M + 1, 100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Synthesis, and Preclinical Evaluations of Novel 4-Substituted
1,5-Diarylanilines as Potent HIV-1 Non-Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase
Inhibitor (NNRTI) Drug Candidates
