$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of 3 Potassium
carbonate (3 mmol), and dihalide 2 (6 mmol), and DMF (1 mL) were added in
this order to a two-necked flask equipped with a reflux condenser at
15°C. A DMF solution (4 mL) of (S)-binaphthol (1.1 mmol) was added to
this solution over 1 h. After addition, the mixture was stirred 8 h under
reflux. The reaction mixture was quenched by pouring it into water. The
precipitate was collected by suction filtration, washed with water, and
dried under reduced pressure. The solid was purified by silica-gel column
chromatography (CHCl3/hexane = 2:1) to afford the corresponding dihalide
3. 3d, yield 80% [φ]25D: -32; 1H NMR δ (300 MHz, CDCl3): 6.77 (4H, d, J =
8.7 Hz), 7.15 (2H, d, J = 9.0 Hz). 7.20-7.30 (4H, m), 7.40 (2H, d, J =
8.7 Hz), 7.45 (4H, d, J = 8.7 Hz), 7.64 (4H, d, J = 8.7 Hz), 7.80 (4H, d,
J = 8.7 Hz), 7.86 (2H, d, J = 9.0 Hz), 7.89 (2H, d, J = 9.0 Hz) ppm. 13C
NMR δ (75 MHz, CDCl3): 1181.1, 119.6, 122.7, 125.6, 125.7, 127.1, 128.2,
128.9, 129.5, 129.6, 130.5, 131.0, 133.8, 134.6, 139.7, 140.4, 150.6,
161.6 ppm. IR ν (neat): 1012, 1154. 1245, 1323 cm-1. Anal. calcd. for
C44H28Cl2O6S2: C. 67.09; H, 3.58. Found: C, 67.11: H, 3.50%.
