$DATUM Bisacetophenone Oligomer 10. A solution of monomer 7 (1.111 g, 3.00
mmol), 4-fluoroacetophenone (0.967 g, 7.00 mmol), potassium carbonate
(0.967 g, 7.00 mmol) in DMF (10 mL) was stirred at 150°C under nitrogen
atmosphere. After 18 h, the red solution was cooled and poured in water.
The resulting white precipitate was filtered, and dried under vacuum at
80°C (1.454 g, 80% yield). Mp: 263°C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3/TFA 6:1, δ):
2.70 (6H, s, CO-CH3), 7.05 (16H, AA′XX′, Ar), 7.58 (4H, d, Ar), 8.02 (4H,
d, Ar). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3/TFA 6:1, δ): 25.6, 116.8, 119.0, 120.5,
122.0, 128.3, 129.9, 131.9, 136.0, 150.2, 154.2, 156.4, 164.1. IR (KBr):
ν C-H 3043 cm-1, ν C-O 1678 cm-1, ν C-C 1600 cm-1, ν C-O-C 1112 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
