$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 4-hydroxybenzoate (7.6 g, 50 mmol) was dissolved in
N,N-dimethylacetamide (50 ml). Anhydrous K2CO3 (10.4 g, 75 mmol) was
added, followed by p-fluorobenzaldehyde (6.29 g, 50.7 mmol). The mixture
was heated to 150°C and stirred under N2 for 3 h. The reaction mixture
was cooled to room temperature and was poured onto ~ 300 g of crashed
ice. The aqueous was carefully adjusted to pH 1-2 with 6 M HCl and
diluted with 500 ml of water. The product was recovered by filtration and
dried on high vacuum overnight. The crude material was purified by flash
chromatography on silica (EtOAc/hexanes, 15%-33%). Methyl
4-(4-formylphenoxy)benzoate (10.18 g, 80%) as a white powder. 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.93 (s, 3H), 7.10 (d, 2H, J= 8.4 Hz), 7.14 (d, 2H, J= 8.7
Hz), 7.90 (d, 2H, J= 8.3 Hz), 8.08 (d, 2H, J= 8.4 Hz), 9.96 (s, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
