$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,6-Bis(4-(p-tolyloxy)phenyl)-4H-pyran-4-one (5). To a 100-mL
three-necked flask equipped with a mechanical stirrer, nitrogen gas
inlet, Dean-Stark trap and reflux condenser, 2 mmol of
2,6-bis(4-fluorophenyl)-pyran-4-one (4), 4 mmol of p-cresol and 7 mmol of
potassium carbonate in 8 mL of NMP/toluene (50% v/v) were added. The
solution was heated to 130-135°C for 2 h to remove water as a
toluene/water azeotrope. The toluene was subsequently removed, and the
reaction mixture was heated to 175- 180°C for 16 h under a nitrogen
atmosphere. Upon completion, 150 mL of methanol was added, and a solid
precipitated out of solution. The precipitate was filtered and washed
thoroughly with distilled water.
2,6-Bis(4-(p-tolyloxy)phenyl)-4H-pyran-4-one (5). Yield 79%. M.p.: 64°C
(decompose). 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm), 7.79-7.77 (4H, m);
7.21-7.19 (4H, m); 7.07-7.05 (4H, m); 7.00-6.97 (4H, m); 6.72 (s, 2H);
2.37 (s, 6H). 13C-NMR (100.1 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm), 180.59, 166.20;
161.35; 153.40; 134.58; 130.82; 127.91; 125.61; 120.33; 118.09; 110.50;
21.08. EI-LRMS m/z: 460 (M+, 71), 432 (100), 211 (28), 208 (13), 91 (15),
69 (19). FTIR [Wavenumbers (cm-1)]: νC=O: 1645; νAr C=C: 1499; νC-O:
1246.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dean-Stark trap used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Functional Aromatic Polyethers: Polymers with Tunable Chromogenic and
Fluorogenic Properties
