$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Table 3: A mixture of 2
mmol of aryl bromide, 3 mmol of phenol, 4 mmol of Cs2CO3, 0.2 mmol of
copper catalyst, 0.6 mmol of N,N-dimethylglycine hydrochlroide salt, and
4 mL of dioxane in a sealed tube was heated at 90 °C under nitrogen
atmosphere. After the reaction completed monitored by TLC, the cooled
mixture was partitioned between ethyl acetate and water. The organic
layer was separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl
acetate.The combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over
Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residual oil was loaded on a
silica gel column and eluted with ethyl acetate/petroleum ether (1/30) to
afford the product. 2,4-Dimethyl-1-p-tolyloxybenzene 24, yield 79%. 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 2.20 (s, 3H), 2.31 (br s, 6H), 6.78 (m, 3H), 6.95
(m, 1H), 7.06 (m, 3H); MS m/z 212 (M+), 197, 179, 169, 154, 120, 105, 91,
77, 65, 51, 41; Anal. Calcd. for C15H16O requires C: 84.87, H: 7.60,
found C: 84.87, H: 7.79.
